course: dictionary
lesson: 9937
title: One word, different meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word tar is one of them. Context, the words around it, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «The workers spread hot tar on the road before the stones went down.» Road and spread tell you that tar is the thick black stuff used to build roads.
explain: Tar can also be a harmful thing. «Cigarette smoke leaves sticky tar in the lungs and damages them.» Here nobody is building anything. The words lungs and damages tell you that tar is a dangerous substance that harms the body.
explain: Tar can be a verb too, an action word. «The sailors tarred the ropes to keep them safe from the sea.» Tarred is what they did to the ropes: they covered them with tar. When you meet a new word, ask: what word would fit here, and does my meaning still make sense in the sentence?
fact: Tar is a thick, black, sticky liquid made from coal, wood or oil.
fact: Tar goes hard when it cools, which is why it is used to make roads and waterproof roofs and boats.
fact: «Thousands of Smilodon skeletons were found in the La Brea Tar Pits in Los Angeles.»
fact: In cigarette smoke, tar is a harmful sticky substance that damages the lungs.
fact: «To tar» something means to cover it with tar.
exercise: «The workers spread hot tar on the road before the stones went down.» What is tar in this sentence? | A kind of bird that nests by roads | *A thick, black, sticky liquid that goes hard when it cools | A bright green plant | A soft, white sweet
exercise: «Cigarette smoke leaves sticky tar in the lungs and damages them.» Which part of the body does the tar harm? | *The lungs | The ears | The hair | The knees
exercise: «The sailors tarred the ropes to keep them safe from the sea.» What does tarred mean? | Cut into small pieces | Painted bright red | Washed in cold water | *Covered with tar
test: «At the La Brea tar pits animals got stuck in sticky tar, and the hunters that came to eat them got stuck too.» Where are the La Brea Tar Pits? | In London | In Sydney | In Paris | *In Los Angeles
test: «Tar» can be a verb as well as a noun. To tar something means what? | To cut it open | To wash it with water | To paint it blue | *To cover it with tar
exam: «Tobacco smoke coats the lungs with tar.» What does tar do to the lungs? | It helps them to breathe more easily | *It damages them | It makes them stronger | It makes them warmer
